<h3 id="community-discussion">Community discussion (self-reported, one thread)</h3>
<p>In a 2020 StrongFirst forum thread on getting a first pull-up (<a href="https://www.strongfirst.com/community/threads/trying-to-get-my-first-pullup-help-needed.16956/" rel="nofollow noopener">thread, opened 19 October 2026</a>), one beginner reported a 40-second neutral-grip dead hang. A reply said that past about 30 seconds, more hanging will have "little, if any, effect" on pull-up ability. That is one anecdote, not a norm.</p>
